# band-run.rq — the adjacent-subsumption run derivation (R165, spec
# 2026-09-04-the-run-is-one-band-design.md § 3.3/§ 3.4).
#
# Open-world derivation over the per-page run-evidence graph (the page is the closure
# boundary — one fresh Graph per merge_run_candidates call, exactly as section-repeat.rq,
# classify-kind.rq and grid-region.rq close within their own transient graphs). Two
# ADJACENT ruled bands extend the same run iff one band's set of distinct rounded rule
# x-positions is a SUBSET of the other's, in EITHER direction — a continuation band that
# redraws only some of the table's rules subsumes, and a title band drawn with the
# table's outer rules is subsumed. Adjacency is the tab:prevBandIndex join, never
# arithmetic: every value compared here is a FACT emitted by sectiongraph.run_evidence,
# and this query contains no numeric literal.
#
# This derivation ENUMERATES CANDIDATES AND SETTLES NOTHING. Whether a proposed run is
# actually one table is disposed of by the existing closed-world tiling membrane
# (compile.merged_run_admissible: is_matrix_candidate -> classify_matrix ->
# assert_matrix_region -> region_tiles), on a scratch graph that is discarded on refusal.
# That split is why the derivation is AXIOM under CLAUDE.md §8 and not a NEURAL
# violation: the reading judgement §8 sends to NEURAL is the one that DISPOSES.
#
# A band carrying no rules emits no node at all (run_evidence's honest abstain), so it
# can never appear here and it breaks the chain. The two subsumption legs sit inside ONE
# FILTER and not two UNION branches: a UNION branch is evaluated independently, so ?a and
# ?b would fall out of scope. Each leg is holon-scoped (NOT EXISTS closes WITHIN this one
# page graph while the graph stays open). The reader (merge_run_candidates) assembles the
# derived (?a, ?b) adjacent pairs into maximal contiguous chains.
PREFIX tab: <https://w3id.org/iladub/tab#>
SELECT ?a ?b WHERE {
  ?u1 a tab:RuledBand ; tab:bandIndex ?a .
  ?u2 a tab:RuledBand ; tab:bandIndex ?b ; tab:prevBandIndex ?a .
  FILTER(
       NOT EXISTS { ?u1 tab:bandRuleX ?x . FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?u2 tab:bandRuleX ?x } }
    || NOT EXISTS { ?u2 tab:bandRuleX ?y . FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?u1 tab:bandRuleX ?y } }
  )
}
